    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647-a1">

                <pb facs="0633" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg535"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Norton &amp; Son to Mr. Geldart.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">steamship beatrice.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: We beg to advise that we are just
                    informed that this steamer has discharged all of her Delagoa Bay cargo into
                    lighters at East London, under orders of the British Government, and in
                    accordance with the terms and conditions of the American and African Steamship
                    Line bill of lading, clause 1, the steamship line is relieved of any further
                    responsibility and goods are at the risk and expense of consignees after leaving
                    ship’s side.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norton &amp; Son</hi>,<lb/><signed>Per J. H.
                        B.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
